---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/ui/SectionHeading.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="About" description={`About ${site.name} — ${site.tagline}`}>
  <section class="ambient">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-wide) px-4 pb-12 pt-16 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">About</p>
      <h1 class="reveal mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-6xl" style="--reveal-delay: 60ms">
        I like the problems where the fix has to{' '}
        <span class="text-gradient">survive the people using it.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="reveal mt-6 max-w-(--container-reading) text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted" style="--reveal-delay: 120ms">
        {site.location}. Software engineer at a dental supply distributor, where I built
        the system the business runs on. Before that: a testing bootcamp, a CS degree, and
        a few years running a phone store and a restaurant floor — which turned out to be
        good training for building tools people have to use all day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-wide) px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.4fr_1fr]">
      <!-- Plain prose, deliberately. Recruiters and their screening tools both
           need to parse this, and specifics land harder than adjectives. -->
      <div class="prose-portfolio reveal">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
          I'm the Operations Technology Manager at RMH3 Dental Supply in Chantilly, VA. In
          practice that means I'm the engineer: I designed, built and run <a href="/projects/mhlhub">MHLHUB</a>,
          the internal ERP that replaced SellerCloud, a pile of spreadsheets, and a Gmail
          inbox somebody triaged by hand. It takes orders from six sales channels, keeps
          a 32,000-product catalog in agreement across all of them, reprices every minute,
          buys shipping labels, handles returns, and keeps the books in step with
          QuickBooks. Daily orders roughly doubled while I've been there — from about 270 a
          day to about 520 — without adding people to operations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Almost everything I've built started as something a person was doing by hand.
          Repricing was a spreadsheet someone updated every morning. The inventory sync
          exists because two systems disagreed and somebody had to reconcile them at the
          end of every day. Those are the problems I like — the ones where being subtly
          wrong is worse than being obviously broken, and where the design has to hold up
          when a warehouse picker or a customer-service rep is using it at 4pm on a Friday.
        </p>

        <h2>How I got here</h2>
        <p>
          I grew up in Chantilly and studied Computer Science at George Mason. I paid for
          it by working: first as an associate and then store manager at a T-Mobile
          retailer, where I ran the whole store — staffing, cash, inventory — and beat
          the targets by 30% for months at a time; then as head server at a Korean BBQ
          restaurant in Fairfax while I finished school. Neither job was about software,
          but both were about systems that break when they meet real people, and both
          taught me to care whether the person on the other side of the counter actually
          got what they came for.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2024 I did CYDEO's Software Developer in Test program — Selenium, Cucumber
          and Gherkin, REST Assured, JDBC, Jenkins — which is where the testing habits come
          from. I still reach for a test before I trust a fix, and I'd rather automate
          anything I'd otherwise have to check twice. In 2025 RMH3 Dental brought me on to
          fix their pricing spreadsheet. The spreadsheet became a scraper, the scraper
          became a service, and the service became the ERP.
        </p>

        <h2>What I'm into right now</h2>
        <p>
          Running a fleet of AI coding sessions against one codebase without them
          corrupting each other — the hooks, the coordination layer, the rules files that
          make the dangerous operations impossible rather than discouraged. It changed how
          much one engineer can own, and I wrote it up as <a href="/projects/agent-fleet">its own project</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside work: I played bass and contrabass clarinet through school — marching
          band for four years — and still think in sections and cues more than I'd admit.
          I'm Filipino-American; I understand Tagalog better than I speak it. I like video
          games with friends, 3D printing, and finding a restaurant I haven't been to yet.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="space-y-6">
        <div class="tile reveal p-6" style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
          <p class="eyebrow">Facts</p>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4"><dt class="text-ink-faint">Based in</dt><dd class="text-right text-ink">{site.location}</dd></div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4"><dt class="text-ink-faint">Timezone</dt><dd class="text-right text-ink">{site.timezone}</dd></div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4"><dt class="text-ink-faint">Open to</dt><dd class="text-right text-ink">Backend · full-stack · remote or NoVA</dd></div>
            <div class="flex justify-between gap-4"><dt class="text-ink-faint">Email</dt><dd class="text-right"><a class="text-accent hover:underline" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary text-sm">Get in touch</a>
            <a href={site.resumeUrl} class="btn btn-ghost text-sm">Résumé</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="tile reveal p-6" style="--reveal-delay: 140ms">
          <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4">
            {site.education.map((e) => (
              <li>
                <p class="font-semibold text-ink">{e.title}</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">{e.org} · {e.when}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">{e.detail}</p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="tile reveal p-6" style="--reveal-delay: 200ms">
          <p class="eyebrow">Certifications</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm">
            {site.certifications.map((c) => (
              <li>
                <span class="text-ink">{c.name}</span>
                <span class="text-ink-faint"> · {c.issuer} · {c.id}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <!-- Skills -->
    <section class="mt-20">
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="Toolkit" title="What I work with" lead="Ordered by how often I reach for it, not alphabetically." />
      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {site.skills.map((row, i) => (
          <div class="tile reveal p-5" style={`--reveal-delay: ${i * 50}ms`}>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-faint">{row.group}</p>
            <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
              {row.items.map((item) => (
                <li class="rounded-md bg-surface-raised px-2 py-1 text-sm text-ink">{item}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Timeline -->
    <section class="mt-20">
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="Timeline" title="Experience" link={{ href: '/resume', label: 'Full résumé' }} />
      <ol class="relative space-y-10 border-l border-border pl-8">
        {site.experience.map((job, i) => (
          <li class="reveal relative" style={`--reveal-delay: ${i * 60}ms`}>
            <span
              class:list={[
                'absolute -left-[2.4rem] top-1.5 size-3 rounded-full ring-4 ring-bg',
                i === 0 ? 'bg-accent' : 'bg-border-strong',
              ]}
              aria-hidden="true"
            ></span>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
              <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-ink">
                {job.title} <span class="font-sans font-normal text-ink-muted">· {job.org}, {job.place}</span>
              </h3>
              <p class="text-sm tabular-nums text-ink-faint">{job.start} – {job.end}</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="mt-3 max-w-(--container-reading) space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
              {job.bullets.map((b) => (
                <li class="flex gap-3">
                  <span class="mt-2 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span>{b}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
